 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "Who was sold as a slave, then wrote Don Quixote?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Miguel de Cervantes. Before he wrote the most famous novel in Spanish, his life was its own adventure."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Where does his story start?",
   "scene": "start",
   "date": "1571",
   "place": "Mediterranean"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "At sea. Spain and the Ottoman Empire were fighting for the Mediterranean."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "At Lepanto in 1571, Cervantes, aged twenty-four, took two shots in the chest. A third ruined his left hand.",
   "scene": "lepanto",
   "date": "7 October 1571",
   "place": "Lepanto",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.4,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.6,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And the slavery?",
   "scene": "captive",
   "date": "26 September 1575",
   "place": "Algiers"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Four years later, sailing home, his galley was taken by pirates. He was sold as a slave in Algiers."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "He tried to escape four times. Every time, he took the blame alone.",
   "scene": "algiers",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "After five years, Trinitarian friars raised his ransom and bought him free.",
   "scene": "algiers2",
   "date": "19 September 1580",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.45,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So how did he become a writer?",
   "scene": "seville",
   "date": "1597",
   "place": "Seville",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Slowly. Back home he became a tax collector. Trouble with his accounts landed him in a Seville jail. In the book's prologue, he hinted it was born in a prison."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In 1605 it came out: an old man reads too many knight stories, and rides off to be a knight himself.",
   "scene": "titlepage",
   "date": "1605",
   "place": "Madrid",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "He charges at windmills, sure they are giants. It was a hit at once. We still say tilting at windmills.",
   "scene": "windmills",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.4,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.6,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Is it true he died the same day as Shakespeare?",
   "scene": "shakespeare",
   "date": "April 1616",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.33,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Not exactly. Shakespeare's date, the twenty-third of April, comes from England's old calendar. On Spain's calendar he died eleven days after Cervantes."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And Spain when he died?",
   "scene": "end",
   "date": "1616",
   "place": "Spain"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Still a huge monarchy, from Portugal to Naples. But it had already lost the northern Netherlands."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "And this face? No one knows if it's really him. No portrait of Cervantes is known to be genuine.",
   "scene": "cervantes2",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.33,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Next time: Velázquez, the painter who painted himself. Like the video and follow History Sketches.",
   "say": "Next time: Velasquez, the painter who painted himself. Like the video and follow History Sketches."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And tell us in the comments what you think!"
  },
  {
   "type": "end",
   "text": "Next: Velázquez, the painter who painted himself",
   "sub": "Follow History Sketches"
  }
 ],
